  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "⚔️ Githyanki Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Clipped, harsh githyanki names in the style of Lae'zel, with a rank if you want one."
    },
    "intro": "Githyanki are raiders from the Astral Plane, and their names sound like orders being given. Baldur's Gate 3 made them famous through Lae'zel, and the pattern is easy to hear: short, hard syllables, often split by an apostrophe. This **githyanki name generator** builds names in that style, and can add a rank like kith'rak or gish.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who the githyanki are",
        "content": "<p>In D&D, the githyanki are one half of the gith, a people who once overthrew the mind flayers who enslaved them. After their freedom they split in two: the githyanki, who became warlike raiders, and the githzerai, who turned to discipline and meditation.</p><p>The githyanki live on the Astral Plane, ruled by their undying lich-queen Vlaakith from the city of Tu'narath. They ride red <a href=\"dragon-name-generator.html\">dragons</a> into battle, and their warriors carry the famous silver <a href=\"sword-name-generator.html\">swords</a>. Their hatred of mind flayers drives much of <a href=\"baldurs-gate-3-name-generator.html\">Baldur's Gate 3</a>'s story.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What githyanki names sound like",
        "content": "<p>The githyanki you meet in Baldur's Gate 3 show the pattern: <strong>Lae'zel</strong>, the companion; <strong>Kith'rak Voss</strong>, whose name begins with his rank; and the inquisitor <strong>W'wargaz</strong>.</p><ul><li><strong>Apostrophes</strong> break names into short, clipped parts: Ry'zath, Ka'zira.</li><li><strong>Hard consonants:</strong> k, z, th, v and r, with few soft sounds.</li><li><strong>Short.</strong> Two syllables, three at most. A githyanki name is meant to be barked.</li></ul><p>All the names here are new, so your character won't share a name with someone from the game.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Githyanki ranks",
        "content": "<p>Githyanki society is military, and rank matters. In Baldur's Gate 3, <strong>kith'rak</strong> is a high rank: Kith'rak Voss leads a githyanki patrol hunting for the party. A <strong>gish</strong> is a warrior who also casts spells, the githyanki answer to a fighter-wizard.</p><p>The <strong>With a rank</strong> format puts a rank before the name, as Voss's does. Lower ranks like warrior and knight suit a player character just setting out; kith'rak suits a <a href=\"villain-name-generator.html\">villain</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do githyanki names work?",
        "answer": "They're short and harsh, usually two syllables, often split by an apostrophe, like Lae'zel from Baldur's Gate 3. A rank can go in front, as in Kith'rak Voss."
      },
      {
        "question": "What does kith'rak mean?",
        "answer": "It's a githyanki military rank. In Baldur's Gate 3, Kith'rak Voss is a senior commander."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these in Baldur's Gate 3?",
        "answer": "Yes. Githyanki are a playable race in BG3, and you can type any name in the character creator. Apostrophes are allowed."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's the difference between githyanki and githzerai?",
        "answer": "They were one people, the gith, until they split after escaping the mind flayers. Githyanki became raiders on the Astral Plane; githzerai became disciplined monks in Limbo."
      }
    ]
